WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.039 --> 00:00:04.619
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar, and you're watching "Mind Your Decisions".

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:10.160
I want to thank Omer from Israel for suggesting this type of puzzle.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:17.100
A, B and C play a series of one-on-one basketball games.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:23.720
In a given game, two of them play against each other while the third person rests.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:29.340
The loser of the game then goes to rest while the winner continues to play,

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.180
facing off against the person who just rested.

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:39.059
After they were done, here is how many games each person played

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:46.900
A played in 8 games, B played in 11 games, C played in 15 games

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:52.280
The puzzle is: Who lost the fourth game?

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:59.360
This seems like it will be impossible to figure out, but there is just enough information

00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:07.100
Can you figure it out? Give this problem a try and when you're ready keep watching the video for a solution.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:23.780
So, let's start out with the number of games each person played.

00:01:24.700 --> 00:01:28.720
The first step is to figure out how many games were played in total.

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:36.080
Since each game involves 2 people, if we add up the games played by each person,

00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:39.440
We will double count the total number of games.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:47.320
In other words, the sum of the games listed above is 2 times the total number of games played.

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:54.000
So 2 times the total number of games played is equal to 8 plus 11 plus 15.

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:03.160
We can solve that the number of games played is then one half of 34, which is equal to 17.

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.440
So how does that help us?

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:11.040
Well now, let's consider the minimum number of games played.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:17.180
A person that loses every single game must still play every other game.

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.320
This is because the loser and the resting player rotate with each other.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:30.720
So a person playing in game 1, and then losing all games, will play in all odd-numbered games.

00:02:31.840 --> 00:02:34.460
This is a total of 9 games.

00:02:35.980 --> 00:02:42.860
Similarly, a person playing in game 2, and then losing all games, will play in all even-numbered games.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.800
This will be a total of 8 games.

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:52.020
Now notice, A played in exactly 8 games.

00:02:53.440 --> 00:02:57.360
Logically, 8 games is the minimum number of games a person can play.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:05.220
Since A played in 8 games, we can conclude A played and lost in all of the even-numbered games.

00:03:06.300 --> 00:03:09.620
Thus, A lost the fourth game.

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.200
Amazing!

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.540
Did you figure it out?

